{"id": "EUVD-2026-48926", "enisaUuid": "21a371c6-a62c-36ac-a864-919d7a5aa5cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix double-free in SMB2_open() replay\n\nA response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its\nresponse buffer. If SMB2_open_init() fails before the next send, cleanup\nretains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.\n\nReset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:25", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02bc2896bdc3e29362d6e40d404006944a159c25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3196b5192f246df4272072f61a2f4a3e9967f55d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14498ff5ce0f272ce0ef988721413e06b7038972", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff2d30927bc3bf3c629f0768d2068096e64ef5ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b55e182f2324bc6a604c21a47aa6c448f719a532"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9v59-2cj8-p55r", "CVE-2026-64382"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1051aed2-ce21-3977-8479-d1a36244e094", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "1c0c99af-ec0d-39bd-91b7-5770e1856eaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <3196b5192f246df4272072f61a2f4a3e9967f55d"}, {"id": "37ff2645-e9d8-3018-b53f-2f353e49a39c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <ff2d30927bc3bf3c629f0768d2068096e64ef5ce"}, {"id": "5c2be028-93d9-3abc-b93c-3d43f42037d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.32 <6.6.145"}, {"id": "81678a3c-3751-3531-a0d1-cc5f1f2469d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor":